The Thaana block runs from U+0780 to U+07BF, which is 64 code points. Its assigned characters are the Thaana letters U+0780–U+07A5, the vowel signs and other marks U+07A6–U+07B0, and the letter Naa at U+07B1. That gives 0x7B1 − 0x780 + 1 = 50 assigned code points. U+07B2–U+07BF (14 code points) are unassigned, category Cn.

Unicode 15.1 added no Thaana characters, so the count should be 50 in Python's unicodedata. My main uncertainty is whether I have the exact block boundary right, so I've left a small margin on the 90% interval.

{"estimate": 50, "p50": [50, 50], "p90": [49, 52]}

